  "$comment": "License classification for release/sbom (docs/release/sbom.md). Categories, best to worst: permissive, weak-copyleft, strong-copyleft, network-copyleft, non-osi, proprietary, unknown. An SPDX `OR` takes the best option, `AND` the worst. `first-party` and `not-applicable` are assigned by `annotations`, never by a license string. First-party code is AGPL-3.0-only (everything in this repository: the runtime, the contracts, the apps, the appliance, the hosts service) or proprietary (control, the relay, the update service), Whombat hermes-engine.md HE-63; the annotation comes before its license string, so our own AGPL code is never a third-party network-copyleft row, while AGPL in anyone else's component stays `network-copyleft`. This is an engineering inventory, not legal advice: every flagged row requires qualified review before commercial distribution.",
